   131	### Recency and shared implementation
   132	
   133	- Treat recency weighting as learning: pass policies explicitly and select them only inside prior cutoff windows.
   134	- Policies include equal expansion, time/issue decay, bounded recent-state blends, change detectors, refit cadence, half-life, window, blend, threshold, and ESS floors.
   135	- Receipts must bind the full weight ledger, effective sample size (ESS), long-history shrinkage, and policy parameters.
   136	- Sparse recent evidence must fail closed or shrink to the frozen long-history prior.
   137	- Recent-state blends must equal `(1-alpha) * long_history + alpha * recent_state`, with both distributions normalized and component masses reconciled separately.
   138	- Multiplying recent rows within one global normalization is not an accepted blend.
   139	- All chronology machinery must come from `packages/beidan/inst/python/beidan_backend/temporal_learning`, including R/QMD and imported-function usage.
   140	- Research clients supply domain fit/predict/select callbacks only; do not copy cutoff, availability, partition, weighting, ESS, cache, receipt, runner, or replay utilities.
   141	- New direct historical fitting outside shared learning contexts and duplicated temporal helpers fail governance checks.
   142	- Replace/delete obsolete implementations without compatibility wrappers.
   143	- Static enforcement scans `src/` and `scripts/`; allow legacy debt only by exact AST occurrence fingerprint and count, never whole-file exemptions.
   144	
   145	## Persistent data layer (recorded 2026-10-06)
   146	
   147	- Analytical datasets are Parquet on the NAS at `/mnt/nas/Data/beijing-lot` (CIFS automount; env `BEIDAN_PARQUET_ROOT`); short-lived data stays on NVMe. Read through the package, never by opening files directly: `beidan::read_dataset()` (Arrow, typed, per-file sha256 verified) and `beidan::dataset_query()` (DuckDB, read-only). `dataset_query()` registers **one table per call**, so cross-table joins go in R.
   148	- Single data entry: `beidan_backend.catalog` — `paths.py` resolves roots and `tier:relative/path` tokens, `registry.py` reads `registry/catalog.json` and `schemas/<schema_id>.json`. Roots fail closed when unset or absent; do not add a machine default or a second path convention.
   149	- One version lifecycle for base datasets and derived artifacts: `beidan_backend.versioning.publish_version()` writes `versions/<label>/` and points `current.json` at the newest. Identical content is a no-op; a label already published with different content is refused; refreshing an older label never moves the pointer backwards. `content_digest()` hashes data files only, so a new `generated_at` does not change identity.
   150	- `settlement` = base dataset (19 tables, registered in the version manifest) plus derived `play_labels` (one row per issue/slot/play for all five plays, registered in the catalog, partitioned by `play`). Partition arguments are not interchangeable: `issue_year` selects a base partition, `play` selects a derived shard, `issue` filters rows; misuse stops.
   151	- **This CIFS mount corrupts in-place overwrites.** Writing over an existing file produced zero-padded/truncated results: a Parquet with a zeroed footer, and twice a JSON with trailing NULs. Always write to a temp name, read it back, then rename. `versioning.write_json_atomically()` and `settlement_backfill.write_parquet_atomically()` exist for this; never use a plain `write_text`/`write_parquet` onto an existing path here.
   152	- Sandisk is being physically retired by the owner; the raw capture layer is not retained (derived layers carry sha256 references). Do not add work that depends on the Sandisk disk.
